  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/... \nModels remain in good agreement that the next low pressure system \nwill reach the California coast early Monday and move into the lower \ndeserts by Tuesday morning. Tuesday rain chances will return to the \nforecast with NBM PoPs peaking between 50-80% in south- central AZ \nand the higher terrain areas, while SW AZ PoPs will be 20-40%. Rain \ntotals Tuesday are expected to be between 0.25\"-0.50\" to locally \nhigher (up to an inch) in the higher terrain. By Wednesday models \nare pointing towards yet again another low pressure system moving \ninland from the Pacific NW, however discrepancies between models are \nevident for how this system will track throughout the rest of the \nworkweek. Due to this confidence remains low for PoPs by mid to late \nnext week as things are too inconsistent at this time. \n\nDespite how the mid-week system tracks, a more significant cooling \ntrend can be counted on by the middle of the week as these series of \nweather systems move in from the northwest. They will likely usher \nin a cooler air mass with afternoon highs trending more towards the \nupper 60s to low 70s by late next week, with how much the \ntemperatures cool being dependent on the depth and position of the \nsystems.",
